list.item:
only one countdown decrements per tick, across the whole list — a latch is set by the first entry
that has one, and every later entry is passed over even if it is also counting down. So a queue of three
delays takes their sum, not their maximum;

member.remarks:
The struck bone takes the most of it and its neighbours progressively less, so a body reacts as a
body. Giving the whole impulse to one bone flails that limb about on the end of the torso;
spreading it evenly makes every hit read the same wherever it landed.

remarks.code:
if (camera[452] != 0.0) {
    s = sin(camera[456]);
    z          += camera[452] * s;          // the camera's world-space height
    rigOffset   = camera[452] * 0.075 * s;  // the first-person rig follows at 7.5%
    camera[456] += 0.20943952;
    if (camera[456] >= 3.1415927) camera[452] = 0.0;
}

remarks.para:
Three ways out give a zero correction, and all three are the original's: the clip does not travel;
none of the nine rays met anything; or the nearest obstruction is further than the extended
reach, in which case there is nothing to correct for.

A vehicle's guns are attachments of its model (0x4F4800 spawns them through 0x4C4950);
each TASKTYPE_AISTATIONARYGUN names its weapon by model (0x413C00). A gun mounted on
another gun -- a T80's coaxial M2HB on its turret -- sits at the sum of both attachment offsets.
